  {:title
   "tui-emit's `printed` counter is never reset on a mid-turn stream failure, so the next turn's reply silently loses its first N characters and its 'assistant ' label",
   :file "packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/infra/cli/tui_repl.cljs",
   :detail
   "`printed` is created once per REPL session (line 49) and is only reset at :turn_end when pos? (line 72). A mid-stream failure is reachable: the SSE reader's `.read` in pull-network! (packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/extern/openai.cljs:183) is unguarded, so a dropped connection after deltas were streamed rejects `.next`, throws out of loop/run-loop (loop.cljs:29), and lands in run-tui-repl's catch (tui_repl.cljs:123-126), which clears the indicator and prints 'Turn error:' but leaves `printed` at, say, 120. On the next user turn, message_update text shorter than 120 fails `(> (count text) @printed)` so nothing is written; once it exceeds 120, `(subs text @printed)` (line 61) drops the first 120 chars of the new reply and `(zero? @printed)` (line 59) is false so the 'assistant ' label is never printed. The corruption self-heals at that turn's :turn_end, but one reply is silently truncated. Fix direction: reset `printed` in the catch path, or scope it per-turn by resetting on :turn_start.",
   :severity "should-fix",
   :card "differential-render-host",
   :lens "correctness",
   :survives false,
   :reasons
   ["The mechanics check out (verified end-to-end: `printed` atom at tui_repl.cljs:49 persists across turns and resets only at pos? `:turn_end` :70-72; the SSE `.read` at openai.cljs:183 is unguarded — only the initial post-chat is wrapped, :292-303 — so a mid-stream drop rejects `.next` at loop.cljs:29, propagates out of run-loop into the tui_repl catch :123-126, which prints 'Turn error:' without resetting `printed`; the next reply's echo then loses its first N chars and its label, self-healing at that turn's `:turn_end`). But the finding is refuted on two independent grounds. (1) Out of scope: the `printed`-counter streaming-render machinery is the delivered feature of card ai-cljs-rewrite-phase-3-extern-openai (status: done), whose delivery notes explicitly claim 'eta-mu.infra.cli.tui-repl streams raw text via the terminal boundary and only falls back to the boxed/wrapped renderer when nothing was streamed.' The card under review delivered the terminal-ui infra host (diff-ops/render!/resize) plus the 'thinking...' indicator wiring — its scope note names exactly that, and its DoD states '--plain is untouched.' The identical non-reset pattern exists verbatim in repl.cljs:62-82, a file this card never touched, proving the latent behavior belongs to the streaming feature, not the differential-render host. It landed in the same bundled commit 054dd55, but board records assign ownership to the completed openai-streaming card. (2) Not promotion-gating: the trigger is a mid-turn network failure already surfaced to the user as 'Turn error:', the corruption is display-only (context/session messages are intact — the failed turn is discarded and the next turn's full text flows through message events; only the incremental terminal echo is offset), affects exactly one reply, and self-heals. A real but minor, edge-case, self-healing display bug in a different card's already-done feature should be filed as follow-up hardening (e.g., reset `printed` on :turn_start or in the catch path) against the streaming surface, not gate this card's review→done promotion."
    "Claim verified line-by-line against the code. (a) tui_repl.cljs:49 creates `printed` once per session (tui-emit is invoked once at line 101) and it is reset only at :turn_end when pos? (line 72). (b) The failure path is real: openai.cljs:183's `await (.read reader)` in pull-network! is unguarded — stream-chat's try/catch (lines 292-303) wraps only the initial post-chat, not the returned sse-stream's .next/.result — so a mid-stream connection drop rejects through stream-next!/drain-events!, through loop.cljs:29's unguarded `await (.next stream)` (run-loop has no catch), into run-tui-repl's catch (tui_repl.cljs:123-126), which prints 'Turn error:' but cannot touch the closed-over `printed`. No :turn_end is emitted for the failed turn (the throw bypasses loop.cljs:213/225/238), so `printed` stays stale (e.g. 120). (c) Next turn: cumulative :message_update text ≤ stale count fails `(> (count text) @printed)` so the reply prints nothing at all (turn_end then emits a bare newline and resets — a fully invisible reply); longer text prints only `(subs text @printed)` with no 'assistant ' label. Self-heals after one corrupted turn, exactly as described. (d) Not grandfathered: `git show 054dd55` (this card's own delivery commit, dated 2026-07-16, 'terminal-ui infra host') introduced the `printed` atom and the entire :message_update raw-streaming path — the pre-image of tui-emit had no streaming and no `printed`. The bug is in code this card delivered. (e) Not documented as a tradeoff: the card's scope note and board-triage comment cover the alt-screen deferral and thinking-indicator only. (f) Not minor: silent loss of a complete assistant reply (or truncation without label) after a routine network hiccup, in the primary user-facing surface of a P0 card, with a one-line fix (reset `printed` on :turn_start or in the catch path). The finding survives: real, in-scope, promotion-gating."]}
  {:title
   "Same delivering commit adds raw js/process.stdout writes in eta-mu.infra.cli.repl, outside extern.*",
   :file "packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/infra/cli/repl.cljs",
   :detail
   "DoD item 4 ('No raw Node/terminal interop outside extern.*') is satisfied by the card's own code (host.cljs requires only extern.terminal, host.cljs:10; tui_repl.cljs reaches the terminal only via eta-mu.terminal-ui.extern.terminal and input via eta-mu.extern.readline). However, commit 054dd55 — the commit delivering this card — also added new raw interop to the plain REPL: make-repl-emit writes streamed deltas via `(.write js/process.stdout ...)` at repl.cljs:71 and repl.cljs:81 (both are `+` lines in this commit's diff; the pre-existing `.on js/process.stdin` at :142/:145 predates it). eta-mu.extern.process exists as the designated boundary (its ns docstring: 'All direct access to `process` is isolated here') but exposes no stdout-write wrapper, and AGENTS.md's construction order states 'Nothing above extern touches a raw host object.' Under a card-scope-only reading of DoD 4 the item is met; under a whole-commit reading it is newly violated. A maintainer should decide whether the honest fix is a stdout write fn in eta-mu.extern.process used by make-repl-emit, or an explicit note on the card that DoD 4 covers only the host/tui-repl diff.",
   :severity "should-fix",
   :card "differential-render-host",
   :lens "dod-coverage",
   :survives false,
   :reasons
   ["The claim's narrow facts are accurate but its framing fails on scope and documented intent. (1) Wrong card: the raw `.write js/process.stdout` lines in repl.cljs were explicitly delivered by a different card — `ai-cljs-rewrite-phase-3-extern-openai` (SSE streaming), whose own comment history (card line 104) documents the decision: 'eta-mu.infra.cli.repl (--plain) now writes text deltas directly to process.stdout as they arrive (bypassing println, since this runtime's *print-fn* is console.log-based and would inject a stray newline per call)'. That is a deliberate, documented tradeoff with a stated rationale, mirrored in the make-repl-emit docstring itself. (2) 'Same delivering commit' is an artifact: 054dd55 is a Π fork-tax mega-snapshot delivering 5+ independent work streams (openai extern, tool registry law, agent e2e, terminal-ui host, find/glob/grep/ls tools); co-location in a snapshot commit does not put another card's code into this card's diff. (3) The claim concedes the only reading that matters for promotion: under the card-scope reading of DoD 4 the item is met — this card's delivered surface (terminal-ui host.cljs requiring only extern.terminal, tui_repl.cljs going through terminal-ui extern.terminal and extern.readline) has no raw interop, and the card's scope note explicitly kept `--plain`/repl.cljs out of this card. (4) repl.cljs was never inside the extern boundary to begin with — raw `js/process.stdin` access at :142/:145 predates the commit (grandfathered), so 'newly violated' overstates even the whole-commit reading. (5) The SSE-streaming card's explicit DoD (incremental rendering in both REPLs, delta accumulation, lifecycle events, tests, kondo green) contains no extern-purity gate, so no card's DoD is breached. Whether eta-mu.extern.process should grow a stdout-write wrapper is a legitimate hygiene question for the SSE card or a follow-up, but it is out of this card's delivered scope, already documented as deliberate, and not promotion-gating for terminal-ui-differential-render-host."
    "Factual core is accurate (git diff 054dd55~1..054dd55 confirms `.write js/process.stdout` at repl.cljs:71 and :81 are new `+` lines, and eta-mu.extern.process exposes no stdout wrapper), but the finding fails on scope and documentation grounds. Commit 054dd55 is a multi-card fork-tax snapshot (its own message lists openai extern base-url/auth-token, tool registry law, agent e2e, terminal-ui infra host, and find/glob/grep/ls tools), so a whole-commit reading of this card's DoD 4 is invalid. The repl.cljs make-repl-emit change belongs to a different card — ai-cljs-rewrite-phase-3-extern-openai (SSE streaming) — whose comment history explicitly documents this exact decision: 'eta-mu.infra.cli.repl (--plain) now writes text deltas directly to process.stdout as they arrive (bypassing println, since this runtime's *print-fn* is console.log-based and would inject a stray newline per call).' So the behavior is (a) out of this card's delivered scope, (b) deliberate and documented on the card that owns it, and (c) the claim itself concedes this card's own code (host.cljs, tui_repl.cljs) satisfies DoD 4. Nothing here should gate terminal-ui-differential-render-host's review→done promotion; at most it's a refactor suggestion for the SSE card's surface, where it is already recorded as an accepted tradeoff."]}
  {:title
