   :file
   "packages/eta-mu/src/cljs/eta_mu/infra/cli/commands/agent.cljs",
   :detail
   "The TTY half of DoD 3 rests on artifacts except its final live check: routing exists in code (agent.cljs:88-91, TTY → tui-repl/run-tui-repl, --plain → repl/run-repl) and the thinking-indicator show/clear has a unit test (tui_repl_test.cljs:56-74). But no automated test exercises the `(process/stdin-tty?)` true branch: agent_cli_e2e.cljs spawns the CLI with `:stdio \"pipe\"` and prompt args (single-turn path), and agent_test.cljs only covers single-turn-with-args and run-repl directly. The 'verified with `script` in a real pty' claim (card lines 86-89) has no captured pty transcript or log committed anywhere in the repo (grep for script/cat -A artifacts finds only the card text itself). This matches the DoD's stated method and repo precedent (predecessor terminal-ui-cljs-package used the same manual script method and was promoted), so it is not a process violation — but the TTY branch could silently regress (e.g. routing flip) with no test failing.",
   :severity "nit",
   :card "differential-render-host",
   :lens "dod-coverage",
   :survives false,
   :reasons
   ["Factually accurate but non-gating by the finding's own admission and by the card's explicit terms. Verified: agent.cljs:88-91 does route TTY→tui-repl / --plain→repl, the thinking-indicator has a unit test (tui_repl_test.cljs:56-74), and the e2e suite (test-e2e/cljs/eta_mu/e2e/agent_cli_e2e.cljs:130) spawns with :stdio \"pipe\", so the (process/stdin-tty?) true branch indeed has no automated coverage and no pty transcript is committed. However: (1) DoD 3 as written specifies exactly this verification method — 'verified with `script` to allocate a real pty, same method used in the predecessor card' — and the scope note (lines 86-89) documents that the manual pty run was performed, including the `cat -A` evidence of \\r+[K clearing the indicator in place; committing the transcript was never a DoD requirement. (2) The claim itself concedes 'this matches the DoD's stated method and repo precedent (predecessor used the same manual script method and was promoted), so it is not a process violation' and self-labels severity 'nit'. (3) An automated pty harness is out of this card's delivered scope: the scope note explicitly deferred the full raw-mode terminal takeover — the natural home for pty-level automation, since driving a real pty against readline's cooked-mode input is precisely the raw-mode-vs-readline conflict — to terminal-ui-input-editor. (4) The card's board triage (line 115) re-verified all gates green (terminal-ui 37/37, eta-mu 116/116, e2e 3/3, kondo 0/0) and recommends promotion. A self-described nit that admits compliance with the card's stated DoD method and repo precedent, and whose requested remedy belongs to a successor card, cannot gate a review→done promotion."
    "The finding is factually accurate but self-defeating as a gating issue. The DoD item it critiques (card lines 52-55) explicitly names 'verified with `script` to allocate a real pty, same method used in the predecessor card' as the acceptance method — manual pty verification without a committed transcript IS the specified, documented acceptance criterion, not a deviation from it. The scope note (lines 86-89) records precisely what was manually verified and how (`cat -A` showing \\r + [K before replacement text). The reviewer concedes this 'matches the DoD's stated method and repo precedent... so it is not a process violation,' leaving only a hypothetical future-regression concern (routing flip) rated nit. Verified the code: agent.cljs:84-94 routes TTY→tui-repl, --plain→repl, piped→run-piped-input; tui_repl_test.cljs exercises run-tui-repl directly (3 tests) and the eta-mu suite is 116/116 green per the card's re-verified triage note. Adding automated pty-spawning coverage was never in this card's scope (scope is the differential-render host + thinking indicator; the full terminal takeover is explicitly deferred to terminal-ui-input-editor). A nit-level test-gap observation against a documented, precedent-backed manual acceptance method is not promotion-gating."]}]}
